  "changes": [
    "Automatic CRT signals fit at least three final display rows per signal line, within existing quality budgets: up to 240 lines in a 720-row window, 360 at 1080, 480 at larger sizes. 3D world resolution is independent.",
    "Tape-only processing and explicit custom/source sizing or original supersampling/integer fit retain their sizing. Smaller automatic signals keep tape defect scaling proportional.",
    "EasyMode/Hyllian scanline cutoffs raised from 400 to 1000; calibrated beam strength for their authored looks.",
    "Royale automatic interlace detection disabled for progressive game frames; beam maximum sigma reduced to 0.28. Explicit custom parameter sets remain authoritative.",
    "Crtsim security-monitor raster restored using its native staggered phosphor mask, scale 4, opacity 0.65 and brightness 0.6. Original persistence retained.",
    "Aperture and the Glow models retain their existing beam calibration; their raster benefits from the smaller-window sizing fix.",
    "EasyMode cosine beam receives a tiny positive floor before fractional pow in the generated shader, fixing Metal NaN black rows at exact beam minima. Importer reproduces it; all vendored source files and other generated shader data unchanged.",
    "Game and workshop share calibration. Only exact recognized former defaults/authored model parameter sets migrate on load; deliberately customized models and unrelated graphics settings remain unchanged."
